## Summary

Added /context files subcommand that shows all files the agent has interacted with during the current session, closing a UX gap vs Claude Code.

### Changes made:

1. `src/commands_project.rs` — Core implementation:
   • Added "files" to CONTEXT_SUBCOMMANDS
   • Added FileAction enum (Read, Edited, Written, Listed, Searched) with labels and emoji icons
   • Added extract_context_files() — parses AgentMessage content blocks for `ToolCall variants, extracting file paths from read_file`, edit_file, write_file, list_files, and search tool calls. Returns a `BTreeMap<FileAction, BTreeSet<String>>` (sorted, deduplicated)
   • Added show_context_files() — displays grouped files with color coding and emoji
   • Wired into handle_context() dispatch
   • Added 7 tests: subcommand presence, smoke tests (empty agent, dispatch routing), extraction from real tool call data, deduplication, non-file tool skipping, search-without-path handling, and label/icon correctness

2. `src/help.rs` — Added /context files to detailed help text and summary help listing

3. `README.md` — Updated commands table to include files subcommand

4. `docs/src/usage/commands.md` — Updated command reference

